<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>

    <!--
      TargetFramework is set PER PROJECT here, unlike src/harness, and the split is the whole point
      of this solution existing separately:

        DownloadFeedback        -> netstandard2.0, so `openness-cli` (net48, pinned there by
                                   Siemens.Engineering) can reference it AND a net8.0 caller can too.
                                   A net8.0 library would be unreferenceable from the one tool that
                                   most needs it.
        DownloadFeedback.Tests  -> net8.0, because nothing in the test path is framework-sensitive.

      The library references NOTHING — no Siemens.Engineering, no network, no Portal. A DownloadResult
      is adapted into a plain DTO tree by the caller (see DownloadResultAdapter), which is what lets
      fifteen recorded logs stand in for a device, and what keeps a change here from ever triggering
      the TIA Openness (Path,FileHash) re-approval cycle that a rebuild of openness-cli does.

      Warnings-as-errors matches the other solutions (audit F-37): there is no CI, so the compiler is
      the only thing that notices drift.
    -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
